 "notes": [
  "Packaging data (pinned upstream file blobs, the installation layout, the pipeline and plugin allowlists, the config steps and the builder check list) is packaging.json; check_recipe.py carries the SHA-256 of packaging.json and upstream-options.json, so the build record binds them through check_recipe.py.",
  "Every one of the 105 option() of the pinned tree is set (upstream-options.json, check_recipe.py check). ON: only the receive-only plugin allowlist (receive-only-policy.json components.satdump.allow_plugins), BUILD_OPENMP and ENABLE_INSTALL; PLUGINS_ALL, the GUI, ZIQ, OpenCL, crashdump, I18N, every hardware SDR source, every audio sink and every app are OFF; PLUGIN_SIMD_NEON stays OFF until a CPU measurement on the Q6A.",
  "EXTERNAL_PLUGINS (a STRING cache entry, upstream default empty in plugins/CMakeLists.txt, bound by its blob) is not passed: the builder never overrides with an empty value.",
  "No libarmadillo-dev: find_package(Armadillo) is optional at 1aedd60 (src-core/CMakeLists.txt:141) and leaving it out keeps configure deterministic; no libzstd-dev (BUILD_ZIQ OFF), no SDR, USB or audio development packages.",
  "Patch 0004 removes upstream's -march=native: the builder's clean environment never defines CI, so CMakeLists.txt:166-172 would target the CI runner's CPU instead of the QCS6490 and replace CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS (dropping -fopenmp).",
  "Patch 0005 makes IersDBHandler::updateIERS return before its downloads: SatDump 1aedd60 schedules the IERS / leap-second fetch at every start (src-core/db/iers/iers_handler.cpp:33-52) and the task is due at once with the empty database of a private HOME. The decode unit has no network anyway; with the patch and kepler_update_interval Never nothing in the core or the seven plugins fetches at start. Only the AWS NAVATT reader reads the IERS table.",
  "One package satdump, no -dev package: the package hook removes usr/include, the desktop file and the icons; the installation record binds the whole file set as one unit (software/DECODERS.md).",
  "libsatdump_core.so and the plugins have unversioned SONAMEs: dpkg-shlibdeps ignores unversioned libraries it cannot map (dpkg 1.22.6 scripts/dpkg-shlibdeps.pl, read 2026-11-07), so Depends comes from the noble libraries only.",
  "CI evidence only: the runtime check (runtime_check.py) runs in the sr-rx-packages runtime chroot; the LRPT fixture rows stay BLOCKED_NO_LICENSED_FIXTURE and live-localhost PENDING_DEVICE; nothing here is REVIEWED.",
  "Pinned recipe files (SHA-256; the installation record's recipe_sha256 binds them through this note): check_recipe.py 96eefe9bc9fcca73cfc017c33357d867c19629281abbf9797574752e8d1cae5f, packaging.json 3151b89c4029f7d7b28ad4abb78b78d4941418c0029165db8e9f4a7fee60343f, upstream-options.json 923f48f0f1a487c50c5259baf75b5a5fd2c0d2326d3ef68b7fb259911e4fec5c"
 ],
